    {
      "path": "index.html",
      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Pixel Calculator</title>\n  <style>\n    :root {\n      --bg: #1e1e2e;\n      --card: #2a2a3c;\n      --accent: #f9a826;\n      --text: #e0e0e0;\n      --border: #4a4a5e;\n    }\n    * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      min-height: 100vh;\n      display: flex;\n      align-items: center;\n      justify-content: center;\n      background: var(--bg);\n      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      color: var(--text);\n      padding: 16px;\n    }\n    .card {\n      background: var(--card);\n      padding: 24px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n      box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--border), 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 360px;\n      display: flex;\n      flex-direction: column;\n      gap: 16px;\n    }\n    h1 {\n      margin: 0;\n      font-size: 1.5rem;\n      text-align: center;\n      color: var(--accent);\n      letter-spacing: 2px;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n    }\n    .row {\n      display: flex;\n      gap: 12px;\n    }\n    .row > * { flex: 1; }\n    label {\n      display: block;\n      margin-bottom: 4px;\n      font-size: 0.875rem;\n      color: var(--accent);\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 1px;\n    }\n    input, select, button, output {\n      font-family: inherit;\n      font-size: 1rem;\n      padding: 10px 12px;\n      border: 2px solid var(--border);\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      background: var(--bg);\n      color: var(--text);\n      width: 100%;\n    }\n    input:focus, select:focus, button:focus, output:focus {\n      outline: 3px solid var(--accent);\n      outline-offset: 2px;\n    }\n    button {\n      background: var(--accent);\n      color: var(--bg);\n      font-weight: bold;\n      cursor: pointer;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 1px;\n      transition: background 0.1s, transform 0.1s;\n    }\n    button:hover { background: #ffb84d; }\n    button:active { transform: scale(0.97); }\n    output {\n      display: block;\n      text-align: right;\n      font-size: 1.5rem;\n      min-height: 2.5rem;\n      word-break: break-all;\n      background: var(--bg);\n    }\n    @media (max-width: 400px) {\n      .card { padding: 16px; }\n      h1 { font-size: 1.25rem; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"card\">\n    <h1>Pixel Calc</h1>\n    <div class=\"row\">\n      <div>\n        <label for=\"left\">Left</label>\n        <input id=\"left\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" placeholder=\"0\">\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <label for=\"right\">Right</label>\n        <input id=\"right\" type=\"number\" step=\"any\" placeholder=\"0\">\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div>\n      <label for=\"operation\">Operation</label>\n      <select id=\"operation\">\n        <option value=\"add\">Add (+)</option>\n        <option value=\"subtract\">Subtract (−)</option>\n        <option value=\"multiply\">Multiply (×)</option>\n        <option value=\"divide\">Divide (÷)</option>\n      </select>\n    </div>\n    <button id=\"calculate\" type=\"button\">Calculate</button>\n    <div>\n      <label for=\"result\">Result</label>\n      <output id=\"result\" aria-live=\"polite\">0</output>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n  <script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "path": "script.js",
      "content": "document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {\n  var leftInput = document.getElementById('left');\n  var rightInput = document.getElementById('right');\n  var operationSelect = document.getElementById('operation');\n  var calculateButton = document.getElementById('calculate');\n  var resultOutput = document.getElementById('result');\n\n  function showError() {\n    resultOutput.textContent = 'Error';\n  }\n\n  function calculate() {\n    var leftValue = leftInput.value.trim();\n    var rightValue = rightInput.value.trim();\n\n    if (leftValue === '' || rightValue === '') {\n      showError();\n      return;\n    }\n\n    var left = Number(leftValue);\n    var right = Number(rightValue);\n\n    if (!Number.isFinite(left) || !Number.isFinite(right)) {\n      showError();\n      return;\n    }\n\n    var operation = operationSelect.value;\n    var result;\n\n    switch (operation) {\n      case 'add':\n        result = left + right;\n        break;\n      case 'subtract':\n        result = left - right;\n        break;\n      case 'multiply':\n        result = left * right;\n        break;\n      case 'divide':\n        if (right === 0) {\n          showError();\n          return;\n        }\n        result = left / right;\n        break;\n      default:\n        showError();\n        return;\n    }\n\n    if (!Number.isFinite(result)) {\n      showError();\n      return;\n    }\n\n    resultOutput.textContent = String(result);\n  }\n\n  calculateButton.addEventListener('click', calculate);\n\n  [leftInput, rightInput, operationSelect].forEach(function (element) {\n    element.addEventListener('keydown', function (event) {\n      if (event.key === 'Enter') {\n        calculate();\n      }\n    });\n  });\n});",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Calculator\n\nA simple, offline pixel-style calculator for two numbers.\n\n## Features\n\n- Input two numbers (left and right), supporting negative values.\n- Choose an operation: add, subtract, multiply, or divide.\n- Click **Calculate** (or press Enter in any input) to see the result.\n- Errors are shown as `Error` when:\n  - Either input is empty.\n  - Either input is not a finite number.\n  - Division by zero is attempted.\n- The result is displayed as a plain number (no label).\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open `index.html` in any modern browser.\n2. Enter numbers in the **Left** and **Right** fields.\n3. Select an operation from the dropdown.\n4. Click **Calculate**.\n5. The result appears in the **Result** output area.\n\n## Keyboard Accessibility\n\n- All controls are reachable via Tab.\n- Pressing Enter while focused in an input or the operation select triggers calculation.\n- Focus indicators are visible.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- No external dependencies, packages, or network requests.\n- Pure HTML, CSS, and plain JavaScript.\n- Under 200 lines of code.\n- Responsive down to 360px width.\n- No storage used.\n",
      "description": ""
    }
